      "solution": "$\\sin \\theta = \\frac{4}{5}$.\\\\Now $\\cos^2 \\theta + \\sin^2 \\theta = 1$\\\\$\\therefore \\cos^2 \\theta + \\left(\\frac{4}{5}\\right)^2 = 1$\\\\$\\therefore \\cos^2 \\theta + \\frac{16}{25} = 1$\\\\$\\therefore \\cos^2 \\theta = \\frac{9}{25}$ \\\\$\\therefore \\cos \\theta = \\pm\\frac{3}{5}$",
