      "solution": "$\\cos \\theta = -\\frac{2}{7}$.\\\\Now $\\cos^2 \\theta + \\sin^2 \\theta = 1$\\\\$\\therefore \\left(-\\frac{2}{7}\\right)^2 + \\sin^2 \\theta = 1$\\\\$\\therefore \\frac{4}{49} + \\sin^2 \\theta = 1$\\\\$\\therefore \\sin^2 \\theta = \\frac{45}{49}$ \\\\$\\therefore \\sin \\theta = \\pm\\frac{\\sqrt{45}}{7}$",
